 "summary": "Searches of Mathlib and TauCeti turned up no existing version of Milman's converse, and no compactness result for the convex hull of a union beyond the finite-set case (`Set.Finite.isCompact_convexHull`) and the finite-dimensional `IsCompact.convexHull`. The new lemmas build on `IsCompact.convexJoin`, `convexHull_union`, `extremePoints_convexHull_subset` and `LocallyConvexSpace.convex_basis_zero`; neither Mathlib nor TauCeti has a closed-convex neighbourhood basis that would replace the hand-built `closure U\u2080` step.",
